**Given:**

Radius of the first circle (r₁) = 32 cm

Radius of the second circle (r₂) = 8 cm

Distance between the centers of the two circles (AB) = 30 cm

**Formula used:**

Length of the direct common tangent (L) is given by:

L = sqrt{d² - (r₁ - r₂)²}

**Calculations:**

Substitute the given values:

⇒ L = sqrt{30² - (32 - 8)²} 

⇒ L = sqrt{900 - (24)²} 

⇒ L = sqrt{900 - 576} 

⇒ L = sqrt{324} 

⇒ L = 18 cm

**∴ The length of CD is 18 cm.**

